## Recommended architecture for team discussion

Use a **Windows Forms App (.NET)** as the Documents Bot, running once per signed-in Windows user as a system-tray application.

- **COM add-in → Bot:** Windows Named Pipes
- **PWA → Bot:** secure localhost API plus WebSocket
- **PWA → Bot fallback:** backend command through SignalR
- **Bot → Corto backend:** authenticated HTTPS APIs and SignalR
- **Bot → S3:** preferably presigned URLs issued by the backend
- **Bot local state:** SQLite
- **Bot filesystem monitoring:** `FileSystemWatcher` plus scheduled reconciliation

```mermaid
flowchart TB
    PWA["Corto PWA"] <-->|"Local HTTPS + WebSocket"| Bot["Documents Bot"]
    Addin["Word / Outlook COM add-in"] <-->|"Named Pipe"| Bot
    PWA <-->|"HTTPS + SignalR"| API["Corto backend"]
    Bot <-->|"HTTPS + SignalR"| API
    Bot <--> Files["Local matter folders"]
    API <--> S3["S3 provider"]
    Bot <--> DB["Local SQLite"]
```

The backend remains the authoritative source of document metadata and versions. The Bot is responsible for local filesystem operations and background synchronization.

This new synchronization must only activate for **S3-backed matters**. OneDrive and other providers must continue using their existing integration so that files are not synchronized twice.

