## Decisions the team should make first

Before implementing the full backlog, agree on:

1. WinForms versus WPF for the tray UI.
2. Whether localhost communication is permitted by corporate browser policy.
3. How the localhost HTTPS certificate will be installed and rotated.
4. Whether backend SignalR is fallback-only or the primary PWA command path.
5. Authentication/device-pairing flow.
6. Conflict-copy naming and resolution UX.
7. Delete propagation and retention rules.
8. Maximum file size and multipart thresholds.
9. Supported folder types, including network and removable drives.
10. Whether syncing must continue without a signed-in Windows user.

My recommended first sprint would contain **BOT-001 through BOT-005**, followed by **BOT-010, BOT-011, BOT-020 and BOT-050**. That resolves the highest-risk technical questions before committing to the full implementation.
